course: dictionary
lesson: 972
title: Blurriness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Blurriness is a noun. It names the state of being blurry, when things are not sharp or clear, so you cannot see the edges or details well.
explain: Look at the word in parts. Blur means something is not clear, and -iness turns it into a noun, a thing you can name. «Eye drops can widen the pupils so the optometrist can see inside the eye, and the blurriness wears off after a few hours» tells you blurriness is temporary: it goes away.
explain: The clues help again. Wide pupils let in more light, so bright sun can feel dazzling until the blurriness wears off. Ask yourself what word would fit: «the blurriness» could be replaced by «the unclear, fuzzy vision», and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Blurriness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some blurriness, not blurrinesses.
fact: «Blurriness» means the state of being blurry: not sharp or clear.
fact: «Blurriness» can mean unclear vision, when things look fuzzy to your eyes.
fact: «Blurriness» can also mean a lack of clearness in ideas or memories.
fact: In science, an image that is out of focus shows blurriness, and glasses or lenses can fix it. In photos, blurriness often comes from moving the camera.
exercise: «Eye drops can widen the pupils, and the blurriness wears off after a few hours.» What does blurriness mean here? | Bright colours that shine | *Things look fuzzy and not sharp | Feeling sleepy after a long day | A loud noise that goes on and on
exercise: A photo is spoiled because the camera moved. What is the blurriness in the photo? | The picture has too many colours | The picture is very dark | *The picture is not sharp or clear | The picture is printed on paper
exercise: Which word is the noun for the state of being blurry? | blurs | *blurriness | blurry | blurred
test: «The doctor said sudden blurriness in your sight must be checked.» What does sudden blurriness suggest? | *Your vision has suddenly become unclear, so you should see a doctor | You have suddenly grown taller | Your favourite song is playing | You need a new pair of shoes
test: Which sentence shows blurriness of ideas or memories? | The blurriness of the new bike made it fast. | *I have some blurriness about what happened last summer. | She ate a blurriness for lunch. | The blurriness of the bright sun made us hot.
exam: Blurriness is a: | *Noun | Verb | Adjective | Adverb
